# secrets
.env
# built artifacts
db/*.db
# compiled_fs.db is NO LONGER un-ignored here. This file is nested deeper than
# the repo root's, so its `!db/compiled_fs.db` WON — the root added
# `findociq/db/compiled_fs.db` (see the comment there: 215 commits of that 31 MB
# binary are why the clone reached 217 MB) and this stale negation quietly
# cancelled it, leaving the file one `git add -A` from going back into history.
# The durable copy is the GCS bucket:
#   gcloud storage cp findociq/db/compiled_fs.db \
#     gs://findociq-sources-igc2026-team08-6311/db/compiled_fs.db
# ...the v2 clean-schema build (tools/build_compiled_v2.py) IS tracked. 10.5 MB.
# compiled_reload.db, the pass2 replay intermediate it is built FROM, stays
# ignored in the repo-root .gitignore — regenerable and 31 MB.
!db/compiled_v2.db
# durable local before/after snapshots (pre-flight, migrations) -- large binaries,
# referenced by path + sha256 in docs/DECISIONS.md and PROGRESS.md, not git-tracked
db/snapshots/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# parked legacy (kept on disk, not versioned)
_legacy/

# generated discovery outputs (regenerable via pipeline/discover)
data/discovery/

data/review/
out/
